model {
  extend basalt.pool {
    metadata {
      constraint "Only the pool owner can read routing decisions through native authorization and a short-lived signed assertion. Public projection uses current inspectable account mappings; withheld candidates reveal no quota, eligibility, funding or weights. Current targets have explicit freshness and scope, historical decisions have bounded runtime retention, and missing calibration never becomes zero extra accounts. The existing reversible two-choice policy remains authoritative; forecasts and sizing share the pure scheduling replay, while deterministic attention data leaves notification delivery to the editable owner workflow."
    }
  }
}
